From 0644184443027d34c2bfd156387b4b32c30b381e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:47:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] sapphire 1004: Apple80211 capabilities include TKIP (group
 key of WPA/WPA2 mixed networks)

FTTH-KM2T (pair tkip+ccmp, group tkip, psk): wifid stopped after DISASSOCIATE + 422 without ASSOCIATE; a CCMP-only hotspot joined. TopazModem already installs a TKIP group key (s_group_cipher).
---
 bsd/dev/redwood_apple80211.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bsd/dev/redwood_apple80211.c b/bsd/dev/redwood_apple80211.c
index 0cf467b..df93f69 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/redwood_apple80211.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/redwood_apple80211.c
@@ -311,7 +311,12 @@ get(struct apple80211req *request)
 		 * for a WPA2 network ("Unable to join").
 		 */
 		uint8_t bits[13] = { 0 };
-		static const uint8_t has[] = { 2, 3, 6, 9, 10, 14, 17, 19 };
+		/*
+		 * sapphire: also TKIP (1) and TKIP MIC (12). A WPA/WPA2 mixed network with a TKIP group key
+		 * (common on ISP routers) is otherwise never joined: wifid sees a cipher the card lacks and
+		 * stops before ASSOCIATE. The pairwise key stays CCMP; TopazModem installs a TKIP group key.
+		 */
+		static const uint8_t has[] = { 1, 2, 3, 6, 9, 10, 12, 14, 17, 19 };
 
 		for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof(has); i++) {
 			bits[has[i] / 8] |= (uint8_t)(1u << (has[i] % 8));
-- 
